            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0415" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.24/47 Suppl: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-28T19:00:00-04:00">December 28,
                            1942—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>321. Your 401, December 4. You may communicate the following message to President
                    Barclay from President Roosevelt: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I deeply appreciate the decision of the Republic of Liberia to adopt a
                            policy of full collaboration with the United Nations and extend my
                            hearty felicitations on the determination of your Government to lend its
                            aid in combatting and destroying the Axis aggressors. Liberia’s
                            contribution to the common cause will be warmly welcomed.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
